/* Learning Data: Governance on the map, in English: the words of the series' labs (training) and scenarios (evaluation), for its
   three films. Keep the keys in step with learn.es.js. assets/governance-on-the-map/learn.js draws them; "vis" names a picture in
   its PIX, which takes its words from the lab (w) or the scenario (st).
   site-tools/build_series.py reads this file as text (series_learn): "labs:[" and "qs:[" each start a line; each lab's first keys
   are id, kind, film, chapter (a chapter id of its film), c and name, in that order, its id made of letters, digits and _ only; each
   scenario's are type, n (its film's number times ten, plus its place), lab and film. No other object here starts with an id, and
   no other key is called kind or starts an object with type (they're counted).
   Names, numbers and dates follow each film's script (films/governance-on-the-map/<n>-<slug>/script.md): check a film's labs and
   scenarios against it when it changes. Like the films, they draw governance on Noor's map and name no product, file or tool screen.
   close: the series' last words, under the scenarios' results for all films and for the last film: that film's closing chapter
   (chapter), in its own words, and in learn.es.js in its Spanish captions. */
